The level with the Sokoban up stairs is near the Oracle
level.  The Oracle level has a lot of statues that turn into
rocks when broken.  I think this combination is deliberate
on the part of the DevTeam.  You you ran out of rocks
before that monster died, you definitely did not lug 50
rocks with you the first time you ascended into Sokoban.
I carry that many and drop them on the down stairs before
I explore and clear the level.  Then I carry them to the next
level and so on.  I abandon at the top level any that were
not spent clearing monster blocks.

In Nethack sticks and rocks can break my bones but
words can never hurt my.  Spears and arrows are sticks
but blocking monsters like that tend to end up underneath
boulders that plugged the hole.  You can't chat through a
boulder and I'd rather use disposable rocks.


